  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Checked returns are placed on a trolley, and helpers can sort by shelf location or by the age of the return.\", \"decision\": \"How should checked returns be reshelved?\", \"goal\": \"Keep books moving and make the afternoon service easier to use without excluding readers who arrive without an appointment.\", \"problem\": \"A small library becomes crowded during afternoon pickups and returns. It has a request sheet, adjustable pickup windows, a few trained helpers, labeled shelves, and enough room to separate several activities. Staff want a practical plan that preserves walk-in access. Each decision below concerns a different part of the service; none requires exclusive use of all helpers or space.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nHelpers sort the trolley by shelf location and reshelve each location’s checked returns together. Each shelving trip covers a compact part of the library.\nHelpers take the oldest checked returns from the trolley first and follow their shelf locations. Books waiting longest become available again first.\nHelpers divide checked returns into small trolley batches and sort each batch by shelf location before shelving it. Short batches balance prompt return with compact shelving trips."
    }
  ],
